  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math>&nbsp;be any continuous function on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and twice differentiable on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then :",
    "image": null
  },
