  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Let,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></math></p><p>Clearly <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>, will be continuous and twice&nbsp;differentiable on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>By Rolle&#39;s mean value theorem in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>,&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Also, in the interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>&#1472;</mi></msup><mfenced><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>,&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, use Rolle&#39;s theorem on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>,&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;We have,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>&#39;&#39;</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;&#39;</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>,&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;&#39;</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;for some <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p>",
